IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2022 -- PART 1 PRELIMINARY (ss 1 to 3).
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view.  Every answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE):
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE   the text itself says yes / says no on these facts, in the words quoted at that branch
--   NOTHING                  the text does not answer (the reason is tagged `NOTHING-kind (...)` at that branch)
-- A definition that points at another Act (the Employment Claims Act 2016, the Industrial Relations Act 1960, the
-- Employment Act 1968, the State Courts Act 1970), which is not among the sources, is asked as a fact.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary`

-- s 1 (the short title) is machinery and has no rule: see the coverage table in NOTES.md.

§§ `Section 2(1) -- Interpretation`

-- src:105 | 2.—(1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 2(1) (src:105)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the Act's definitions apply` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:106 | “agreed date” means a date specified for the purposes of
-- src:107 | section 7C(2)(a) in a consent form mentioned in
-- src:108 | section 7C(7);
@ref s 2(1) "agreed date" (src:106-108)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the date specified for the purposes of section 7C(2)(a) in the consent form mentioned in section 7C(7)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "agreed date" the date is the agreed date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date specified for the purposes of section 7C(2)(a) in the consent form mentioned in section 7C(7)`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF `the date` EQUALS specified
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“agreed date” means a date specified for the purposes of section 7C(2)(a) in a consent form mentioned in section 7C(7)"
            JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“agreed date” means a date specified for the purposes of section 7C(2)(a) in a consent form mentioned in section 7C(7)"
        JUST FALSE

