-- A contract of service may be written or oral, express or implied: no limb reads how the agreement was made, which
-- is what "whether in writing or oral, express or implied" says.
-- src:125 | “contract of service” means any agreement, whether in writing
-- src:126 | or oral, express or implied, whereby one person agrees to
-- src:127 | employ another as an employee and that other agrees to serve
-- src:128 | his or her employer as an employee;
@ref s 2(1) "contract of service" (src:125-128)
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is express` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one person agrees to employ another as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that other agrees to serve the first as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` MEANS
    IF `one person agrees to employ another as an employee` AND `that other agrees to serve the first as an employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“contract of service” means any agreement ... whereby one person agrees to employ another as an employee and that other agrees to serve his or her employer as an employee"
        JUST FALSE

-- "eligible employee" means an employee who satisfies the criteria in section 7(1): its rule is in the module of Part 3,
-- which holds section 7(1).

-- src:133 | “employee” means a person who has entered into or works under
-- src:134 | a contract of service with an employer;
@ref s 2(1) "employee" (src:133-134)
GIVEN `the person has entered into a contract of service with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person works under a contract of service with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "employee" the person is an employee` MEANS
    IF `the person has entered into a contract of service with an employer` OR `the person works under a contract of service with an employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means a person who has entered into or works under a contract of service with an employer"
        JUST FALSE

-- "means ... and includes": the core is a person who employs another under a contract of service, and the four limbs
-- (a) to (d) are added to it.  Outside both, the text says only "includes", which does not close the class.
-- src:136 | “employer” means a person who employs another person under
-- src:137 | a contract of service and includes —
-- src:139 | (a) the Government;
-- src:141 | (b) any statutory authority;
-- src:143 | (c) any duly authorised agent or manager of any
-- src:144 | employer; and
-- src:146 | (d) any person who owns or is carrying on, or for the time
-- src:147 | being responsible for the management or control of a
-- src:148 | profession, business, trade or work in which any
-- src:149 | employee is engaged;
@ref s 2(1) "employer" (src:136-149)
GIVEN `the person employs another person under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a duly authorised agent or manager of an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person owns, is carrying on, or for the time being is responsible for the management or control of, a profession, business, trade or work in which an employee is engaged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` MEANS
    IF `the person employs another person under a contract of service` OR `the person is the Government` OR `the person is a statutory authority` OR `the person is a duly authorised agent or manager of an employer` OR `the person owns, is carrying on, or for the time being is responsible for the management or control of, a profession, business, trade or work in which an employee is engaged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“employer” means a person who employs another person under a contract of service and includes" limbs (a) to (d); the text does not say that no other person is an employer
        NOTHING

