-- The age specified under section 4(1) that applies to the employee is a fact of the case (the Gazette notification is
-- not among the sources); whether a given age could be so specified is section 4(1), in Part 2.
-- src:170 | “prescribed minimum retirement age”, in relation to an
-- src:171 | employee, means the prescribed minimum retirement age
-- src:172 | specified under section 4(1) that is applicable to the
-- src:173 | employee;
@ref s 2(1) "prescribed minimum retirement age" (src:170-173)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "prescribed minimum retirement age" the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age` MEANS
    employment's `prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- src:177 | “prescribed re-employment age”, in relation to an employee,
-- src:178 | means the prescribed re-employment age specified under
-- src:179 | section 7A(11) that is applicable to the employee;
@ref s 2(1) "prescribed re-employment age" (src:177-179)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "prescribed re-employment age" the employee's prescribed re-employment age` MEANS
    employment's `prescribed re-employment age`

-- "the higher of the following ages applicable to the employee": where no retirement age is stipulated in the contract,
-- only the prescribed minimum retirement age is applicable to the employee, and it is the specified age.
-- src:203 | “specified age”, in relation to an employee, means the higher of
-- src:204 | the following ages applicable to the employee:
-- src:206 | (a) the employee’s prescribed minimum retirement age;
-- src:208 | (b) the retirement age stipulated in the employee’s
-- src:209 | contract of service;
@ref s 2(1) "specified age" (src:203-209)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` MEANS
    CONSIDER employment's `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN employment's `prescribed minimum retirement age`
    WHEN JUST stipulated THEN max (employment's `prescribed minimum retirement age`) stipulated

-- src:183 | “re-employment” means the employment of an employee by the
-- src:184 | same employer on or after the date the employee attains the
-- src:185 | employee’s specified age;
@ref s 2(1) "re-employment" (src:183-185)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the employment is by the same employer as before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the employment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (`s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` employment)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the specified age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN
        IF `the employment is by the same employer as before` AND `the date of the employment` AT LEAST attained
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“re-employment” means the employment of an employee by the same employer on or after the date the employee attains the employee's specified age"
            JUST FALSE

