§§ `Section 2(2) -- treated as dismissed`

-- "(b) the employer retires the employee, or requires or causes that employee to retire or resign on the ground of age".
-- The comma before "or requires or causes" is read as ending the first alternative: "on the ground of age" qualifies
-- requiring or causing the employee to retire or resign, and not the employer's own retiring of the employee (fork F16).
-- src:223 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, an employee is treated as dismissed
-- src:224 | by his or her employer if —
-- src:226 | (a) the contract under which the employee is employed by the
-- src:227 | employer is terminated by the employer, whether it is so
-- src:228 | terminated by notice or without notice; or
-- src:230 | (b) the employer retires the employee, or requires or causes
-- src:231 | that employee to retire or resign on the ground of age.
@ref s 2(2) (src:223-231)
GIVEN `the contract under which the employee is employed is terminated by the employer, by notice or without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer retires the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer requires or causes the employee to retire or resign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requiring or causing is on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) the employee is treated as dismissed by the employer` MEANS
    IF `the contract under which the employee is employed is terminated by the employer, by notice or without notice` OR `the employer retires the employee` OR (`the employer requires or causes the employee to retire or resign` AND `the requiring or causing is on the ground of age`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employee is treated as dismissed by his or her employer if" (a) the contract is terminated by the employer or (b) the employer retires the employee, or requires or causes that employee to retire or resign on the ground of age -- a failed "if" (marginal reading (a))
        JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 2(3) -- attaining an age`

-- src:233 | (3) In this Act, a person is regarded as attaining or having attained
-- src:234 | N years of age (where N is a positive integer) or other higher age on or
-- src:235 | after the Nth or other anniversary (as the case may be) of the date of
-- src:236 | his or her birth.
@ref s 2(3) (src:233-236)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` MEANS
    IF `the age in years` AT MOST 0
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the Act speaks of "N years of age (where N is a positive integer)"; a zero or negative age is not an N
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF DATE_MONTH `the date of birth` EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY `the date of birth` EQUALS 29 AND NOT (`is leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the date of birth` PLUS `the age in years`))
         THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the anniversary of a 29 February birth falls on no date in a year that is not a leap year, and the Act does not say which date stands in
            NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (Date (DATE_DAY `the date of birth`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of birth`) (DATE_YEAR `the date of birth` PLUS `the age in years`))

-- src:233 | (3) In this Act, a person is regarded as attaining or having attained
-- src:234 | N years of age (where N is a positive integer) or other higher age on or
-- src:235 | after the Nth or other anniversary (as the case may be) of the date of
-- src:236 | his or her birth.
@ref s 2(3) (src:233-236)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(3) the person has attained the age on the date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` `the date of birth` `the age in years`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no anniversary date can be worked out for this birth date and age
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST anniversary THEN
        IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST anniversary
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is regarded as attaining or having attained N years of age ... on or after the Nth ... anniversary of the date of his or her birth" -- marginal reading (c)
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 3 -- Officers`

-- Section 3(1) (the officer in charge of the general administration), 3(3) (the Minister's power to appoint
-- investigating officers and other officers) and 3(4) (the Minister's rules for the conduct of officers' duties) are
-- machinery and have no rule: see the coverage table in NOTES.md.

-- A notice, a report or a decision that the Act requires of the Commissioner may be given by one of the named
-- officers, within the limits that may be prescribed (the prescribed limits are not among the sources).
-- src:243 | (2) Any Deputy Commissioner for Labour, Principal Assistant
-- src:244 | Commissioner for Labour or Assistant Commissioner for Labour
-- src:245 | appointed under the Employment Act 1968 may, subject to such
-- src:246 | limitations as may be prescribed, perform all duties imposed and
-- src:247 | exercise all powers conferred on the Commissioner by this Act, and
-- src:248 | every duty so performed and power so exercised is deemed to have
-- src:249 | been duly performed and exercised by the Commissioner for the
-- src:250 | purpose of this Act.
@ref s 3(2) (src:243-250)
GIVEN `the act is done by a Deputy Commissioner, a Principal Assistant Commissioner or an Assistant Commissioner for Labour appointed under the Employment Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is a duty imposed or a power conferred on the Commissioner by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within the limitations that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) the act is deemed to have been duly performed or exercised by the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `the act is done by a Deputy Commissioner, a Principal Assistant Commissioner or an Assistant Commissioner for Labour appointed under the Employment Act 1968` AND `the act is a duty imposed or a power conferred on the Commissioner by this Act` AND `the act is within the limitations that may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for a duty or power "conferred on the Commissioner by this Act" done by one of the named officers "subject to such limitations as may be prescribed"; the case falls outside, or the limitations are in regulations that are not among the sources
        NOTHING
